CHANGE.log: a running log of the changes to SIGKILL, newest first.

Every entry names each contributor with their GitHub login and a linkable X profile, and says how the X handle was checked.
A handle is never guessed; where none can be verified the entry says so. Drafts of the posts that announce changes are in
X-POSTS.html. Contributors from before this log began, and what each made, are in CREDITS.md.

2026-11-14  Merge #1: combat shaders compile as the arena loads (2231d13)
  What: the arena compiles every shader a weapon, an ability or a hit draws only once it is used, as it loads, so the first
        chmod 000 hit and the first /dev/null throw no longer freeze the game for about 1.8 s on a cold start. A cold first
        launch draws its first frame up to 1.6 s later. The fork() shotgun's first long flight can still stall about a second
        (a pipeline the driver builds, not a shader; a separate effort). Check step 75.
  Who:  TechLuddite, https://github.com/TechLuddite, X https://x.com/gh_TechLuddite
        X checked 2026-11-14: his GitHub profile declares it (twitter_username). Plain @TechLuddite is a different account.
  PR:   https://github.com/nixfred/sigkill/pull/1

2026-11-14  Merge #2: gamepad support (5fae38b)
  What: a gamepad plays the arena, the Esc menu, Missions and Loadout: sticks, triggers, face buttons, bumpers and D-pad.
        In split-screen co-op the pad is player 2's alone and player 1 plays on keyboard and mouse (the merge fixed a collision
        in which one pad drove both players). Check step 76.
  Who:  TechLuddite, https://github.com/TechLuddite, X https://x.com/gh_TechLuddite (checked as above)
  PR:   https://github.com/nixfred/sigkill/pull/2

2026-11-14  Credits (016f2f8)
  What: TechLuddite is the seventh contributor in CREDITS.md and in the in-game credits roll, as every contributor who touches
        the code is.
